messages:
alex.cheng: heads up — planning a small capacity bump for inference-sts and a secrets path rename. terraform diff below. want a quick eyeball before i apply later today (canary window ~ 11:30 PT).

mika: sgtm to look. what's the target qps we're protecting for with +2 replicas?

alex.cheng: current steady qps ~ 420 p50 latency 45ms. with burst forecasts we want headroom for 700 qps; moving from 3 -> 5 should keep p50 similar with current resource requests. not trying to change autoscaling yet.

jamie: curious about resource changes — are you bumping cpu/mem too? last time we saw OOMs on a few nodes during probe storms.

alex.cheng: yes small CPU bump from 600m -> 900m and memory 1.5Gi -> 2Gi. keeping readiness probes the same.

samira: quick check: are you also rotating the K8s secret path? i remember we moved some keys to /infra/redwood/inference last month.

alex.cheng: right — terraform rename: secret resource path -> data-redwood/inference. plan shows lifecycle replace on the secret reference but i added a kubernetes_secret data lookup to avoid pod restarts. snippet:

```hcl
resource "kubernetes_deployment" "inference_api" {
  metadata { name = "inference-api" }
  spec {
    replicas = 5
    template {
      spec {
        containers {
          name  = "api"
          image = var.image
          resources {
            requests = { cpu = "900m", memory = "2Gi" }
          }
          env { name = "MODEL_KEY_PATH" value = "/secrets/data-redwood/inference/key" }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

# using data source to read existing secret to avoid rolling update
data "kubernetes_secret" "inference_key" {
  metadata { name = "inference-key" namespace = "platform" }
}
```

mika: nice to see the data source. two questions: 1) are the nodes with this workload on mixed instance pools? if so bumping requests could trigger binpacking. 2) readiness probe timing — maybe increase failure threshold briefly during canary?

alex.cheng: 1) yes mixed pools (g5 + a2). i'm planning to set topologySpreadConstraints to prefer gpu nodes but allow fallback. 2) i can relax readinessProbe.failureThreshold from 3->5 for the first 15 minutes via an annotation-based rollout-hook.

jamie: for the canary, please add a small traffic-weighted split (10% canary). we have the routing policy to route by header X-Infra-Canary. infra-bot can create the canary route if you tag the rollout.

alex.cheng: will do. sample canary plan: 10% -> 50% after 20m -> 100% after 40m if no errors. also i'll add a post-apply smoke test step to hit /healthz and a few longer inference traces.

samira: one more — secrets rotation: ensure the new path has read perms for the serviceaccount. otherwise pods will start but fail on init.

alex.cheng: good catch. iam role binding change is in the same tf module. i added a `google_service_account_iam_binding` for the new secret path.

infra-bot: terraform plan completed for twr/inference (draft). 3 resources will be updated, 1 will be replaced. plan id: tf-2419876543.

mika: looks fine from infra side. watch out for binpack and eviction risk; if nodes fill up, autoscaler might spin up new nodes but that can be slow for gpus. maybe stagger pod updates with maxUnavailable = 1.

jamie: +1 to maxUnavailable = 1 for deployment strategy. for StatefulSet you can use partitioned rollout, but here it's a Deployment so RollingUpdate with maxUnavailable 1 and maxSurge 1.

alex.cheng: thanks all — i'll update the rollout config (maxUnavailable=1, maxSurge=1), add the canary route annotation, and include the serviceaccount IAM bind. tagging @infra-bot to run apply at 11:35 PT if no objections. :thumbsup:

mika: :thumbsup: go for it.

samira: no objections. i'll keep pager on for the window.

jamie: ok, ping me if any unexpected errors in the smoke tests.

alex.cheng: applying in ~10m. will follow up with results and logs.
